# Plays, 8-frame strip over 1s. Top row: three circles (r 8, ink outline) at x=24, 48, 72 on y=20, named a, b, c, each with a rest fill of gold.
# `play to_red` then `play to_blue`: to_red sets fill red on a and b; to_blue sets fill blue on b and c. The last play wins, so in every frame
# the top row reads left to right: red, blue, blue (b is blue, not red; no frame shows gold).
# Bottom rows: two squares 12x12 start at x=12, one at y=52 (green, `early`) and one at y=76 (gold, `late`), each slides 72 to the right over .5s.
# `early` plays at once: the green square slides right in frames 1-4 (x=12, 30, 48, 66), then the anim has ended and it is back at its rest x=12 in frames 5-8.
# `late` plays with start:.5s: the gold square rests at x=12 in frames 1-5 and slides right in frames 6-8, at x=30, 48, 66 in frames 6, 7, 8.
# Undocumented, current behavior: a play that is not `loop` is live only in [start, start+dur); outside that window the node sits at its rest pose.
@target anim/play_order.gif 96x96 fps:8 dur:1s

circle 8 at:24,20 fill:p.gold stroke:p.ink,1 name:a
circle 8 at:48,20 fill:p.gold stroke:p.ink,1 name:b
circle 8 at:72,20 fill:p.gold stroke:p.ink,1 name:c
rect 12x12 at:12,52 fill:p.green stroke:p.ink,1 name:e
rect 12x12 at:12,76 fill:p.gold stroke:p.ink,1 name:l

anim to_red dur:1s
  .a fill:p.red
  .b fill:p.red

anim to_blue dur:1s
  .b fill:p.blue
  .c fill:p.blue

anim early dur:500ms
  .e at:key(0,0 72,0 ease:linear)

anim late dur:500ms
  .l at:key(0,0 72,0 ease:linear)

play to_red
play to_blue
play early
play late start:500ms
